ana-docs: Heads-up — opened a docs PR with a new "WireGuard gateway" example for private/vpc installs. It also adds an FAQ section for NAT64/IPv6 translation edge cases and an airgapped download checksum step. PR: https://git.internal/redwood/docs/pull/8123 :eyes:

sam-ux: Nice. Can you paste the minimal nftables snippet you used for the gateway? want to confirm it won't conflict with our typical SNAT profile.

ana-docs: Sure, here's the minimal example (in the PR too):
```
# nftables: masquerade outgoing from private subnet to public interface
table ip nat {
  chain postrouting {
    type nat hook postrouting priority 100;
    oifname "eth0" ip saddr 10.10.0.0/16 counter masquerade
  }
}
```

mike-infra: Looks good. For IPv6 -> NAT64 note we should highlight that we don't do protocol translation — recommend using a separate NAT64 appliance or gateway and link to a reference. Also call out that prefix discovery may differ per distro.

ana-docs: Added a short paragraph: "Redwood installer does not perform NAT64. For IPv6-to-IPv4 translation use a dedicated NAT64 device (TAYGA, Jool) and ensure /etc/resolv.conf points to the DNS64 resolver." I left a TODO to add distro-specific resolv.conf examples.

lee-engr: For the SDK snippet section, can we include a quick JS example showing MTLS + custom endpoint for private deployments? saves a bunch of follow-ups.

ana-docs: Good call. Drafted this sample in PR:
```js
// connection-check.js - minimal JS SDK mTLS example
const {RedwoodClient} = require('@redwood/infer');
const fs = require('fs');
const client = new RedwoodClient({
  baseURL: 'https://private-redwood.example.internal',
  mTLS: {
    cert: fs.readFileSync('/opt/redwood/certs/client.crt'),
    key: fs.readFileSync('/opt/redwood/certs/client.key'),
    ca: fs.readFileSync('/opt/redwood/certs/ca.pem')
  }
});
(async ()=>{
  const r = await client.ping();
  console.log('ping', r.status);
})();
```

sam-ux: Great. Suggest we also add a one-liner for curl with client certs for quick debug: `curl --cert client.crt --key client.key https://private-redwood.example.internal/health`

tess-qa: QA note — the HSM section needs the PKCS#11 module path examples for both SoftHSM and YubiHSM. I found customers often hit a missing pkcs11 path in the installer.

ana-docs: Added snippet: `pkcs11_module: /usr/lib/softhsm/libsofthsm2.so` and a YubiHSM example `pkcs11_module: /usr/lib/libyubihsm.so`. Also included a short troubleshooting checklist: ensure token initialized, check `softhsm2-util --show-slots` output.

mike-infra: For airgapped installs please call out the checksum step for offline bundles. Can you add the exact sha256 CLI we expect ops to run?

ana-docs: Done. Added: `sha256sum redwood-offline-bundle-1.2.3.tar.gz` and a note to verify the signature using our public key (link to sig key in repo). Also added a small note on handling proxies for the bootstrapper when doing staged downloads.

lee-engr: One more: there's a stale link in the TOC that points to the old "private-connectivity" page — I left a linkfix in the PR, please sanity-check the redirects.

ana-docs: Fixed the TOC link and added a redirect comment.

deploy-bot: build-docs: success (sha: a1b2c3f) — preview deployed to https://docs-preview.internal/6112223333

sam-ux: Reviewed the preview quickly — layout looks fine. Minor nit: the code block language for the nftables snippet is detected as plain text on the site, wrap the block with "nft" or "bash" so syntax highlight picks it up.

ana-docs: Will update.

tess-qa: I'm queued to run a quick smoke where I spin up a small VM and follow the guide step-by-step. If I hit anything I'll post here (timeline: EOD).

mike-infra: Please also add a short migration note for customers moving from iptables -> nftables in our on-prem installer (common question). A single command to translate rules or a link to `iptables-translate` should suffice.

ana-docs: Added migration note and example: `iptables-translate -A POSTROUTING -t nat -j MASQUERADE` and a caution about checking kernel nft support.

sam-ux: Thanks. If QA passes I'll merge after you update the highlight and fix any small wording bits (prob tomorrow AM). :+1:

ana-docs: Thanks everyone — appreciate the quick turns. I'll push the minor fixes now.
